{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1462810-where-i-play-\u201cwhere-i-build\u201d\u2026","id":1462810,"title":"Where I play \u201cWhere I Build\u201d\u2026","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-05T10:42:50-07:00","id":1462810,"title":"Where I play \u201cWhere I Build\u201d\u2026","content":"So, I feel like building some characters and I\u2019d like an outlet as well as some people giving some input. On that basis I\u2019m proposing a thread where I do an example of character creation build for different CofD games with parameters set by users on this site.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s how I see it going:<br /> <br /> 1 - I call a game line.<br /> 2 - first poster names the primary splat. For the avoidance of doubt that will be the first listed in each 2E core book (e.g Clan, Auspice, Guild).<br /> 3 - second poster names the secondary splat. Again, that will be the second set of character types listed in the 2E books (e.g. Covenant, Tribe, Decree).<br /> 4 - third poster names two elements I need to include when designing the character. These can be background elements, personality traits, enemies, friends, a quirk, or a mystery.<br /> <br /> If two people cross over on one of the points above I will choose the first. This is partially about challenging myself to make characters i otherwise would not so I\u2019ll go with whatever is placed in front of me first. I think we could always have more examples of CofD character creation as well, am\u2019 rite?<br /> <br /> <br /> so\u2026 with that said. Onyx Path guys. I give you two days to decide what I\u2019m building for<br /> <br /> Beast!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12472-foozle","name":"Foozle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","